# River plastic inputs — local publication build

This directory builds a reproducible local release of the Lebreton et al. (2017) global river-plastic model from Figshare v6. The user requested local preparation only. Uploads, Source Cooperative account/product creation, Portolan registration and Git pushes are not part of this run.

The source has four points with null emission/runoff estimates (source rows 22271, 36248, 36262, 36276). These remain null, with their geometries and catchment attributes retained. The default style marks them gray.

The analytic GeoParquet preserves all 40,760 source points and 53 fixed-point numeric attributes. It adds a one-based source_row identifier and bbox covering columns, and sorts by Hilbert distance. PMTiles provides annual estimates and selected catchment attributes for visualization; lower zooms thin points and tile geometry is quantized. The full model estimates and uncertainty bounds remain in GeoParquet. The data license is CC BY 4.0, with attribution to Lebreton et al. and the original Figshare data release.

The release bundle has a STAC 1.1.0 / Portolan v0.2.0 catalog, one Collection, README and AGENTS files, a field dictionary, a MapLibre style, a thumbnail and a checksum manifest. All owned data links are relative. No unverified future hosting URLs are registered.

From the repository root:

```sh
uv sync --frozen --project commons/publish/gee-community/products/river-plastic-inputs
npm ci --prefix commons/publish/gee-community/products/river-plastic-inputs
uv run --frozen --project commons/publish/gee-community/products/river-plastic-inputs python commons/publish/gee-community/products/river-plastic-inputs/build.py --output .local/gee-publication/river-plastic-inputs/figshare-v6-r1
uv run --frozen --project commons/publish/gee-community/products/river-plastic-inputs python commons/publish/gee-community/products/river-plastic-inputs/validate.py .local/gee-publication/river-plastic-inputs/figshare-v6-r1 --http --report .local/gee-publication/river-plastic-inputs/validation.json
```

The builder requires committed product inputs and refuses to overwrite an existing output directory. The default source archive is the cached `.local/gee-publication/plastic/PlasticRiverInputs.zip`; `--source` selects another copy. Download the exact archive from https://ndownloader.figshare.com/files/7714864 if needed; the builder verifies its size, MD5 and SHA-256 against source.json. Python dependencies are locked in uv.lock; the native builder requires tippecanoe v2.79.0 and records its binary hash. The Python PMTiles reader is locked; the native pmtiles CLI verifies the archive structure.

The validator independently compares every numeric field and coordinate against the original archive, decodes every maximum-zoom tile, verifies identifiers and display attributes, and runs rashid with the profile schema and local data checks. `--http` starts a temporary loopback server and exercises range/CORS responses and a DuckDB HTTP subset query. DuckDB's matching signed httpfs extension must be installed first if it is not already cached (`INSTALL httpfs`). The loopback test does not certify any future remote host.

Run the second STAC validator against only the STAC documents:

```sh
commons/publish/gee-community/products/river-plastic-inputs/node_modules/.bin/stac-node-validator .local/gee-publication/river-plastic-inputs/figshare-v6-r1/catalog.json .local/gee-publication/river-plastic-inputs/figshare-v6-r1/river-plastic-inputs/collection.json
```

That validator may fetch the declared published schemas. Do not use its formatting flags on a built release because they change manifest-pinned bytes.

For local serving:

```sh
uv run --frozen --project commons/publish/gee-community/products/river-plastic-inputs python commons/publish/gee-community/products/river-plastic-inputs/serve.py .local/gee-publication/river-plastic-inputs/figshare-v6-r1
```

Open http://127.0.0.1:8765/catalog.json with a STAC client. The standalone MapLibre style uses the Portolan relative-PMTiles convention; a PMTiles-aware viewer must resolve that URL and install its PMTiles protocol.

Before a later publication, confirm the owner/product and publishing access, upload into an immutable version/build prefix, verify real anonymous range reads and CORS plus a remote subset query, and then submit the public catalog root to Portolan. Add actual public distribution endpoints to Folia only after they exist. A registry submission needs a public contact email. Those actions remain pending under the user's local-only instruction.
